For each function of module `glom.tutorial` below, write a behavioral contract: inputs (what each parameter means), outputs (what is returned), raises (list of exception TYPE NAMES it can raise, [] if none), side_effects ("none" or a short phrase), invariants (a property that always holds, or ""). Base every field ONLY on the code shown. Return one entry per qualname.

### glom.tutorial.Contact.save
signature: save(self)
    def save(self):
        self.objects.save(self)

### glom.tutorial.ContactManager.all
signature: all(self)
    def all(self):
        return list(CONTACTS.values())

### glom.tutorial.ContactManager.get
signature: get(self, contact_id)
    def get(self, contact_id):
        return CONTACTS.get(contact_id)

### glom.tutorial.ContactManager.save
signature: save(self, contact)
    def save(self, contact):
        CONTACTS[contact.id] = contact
